This parable would be germane if it included the scenario in which
Kennita speculates on Tim's desire to kill her, to squish her like a
bug, and so forth. 

It is true that folks, including myself, are free to ignore the
clueless and boring things they hear. I do this with most of the
clueless on this list. Thus, I am not calling for censorship (not that
Dan has claimed I am).

Rather, when a member of the list launches into a tirade about her
confused feelings that I want to squish her like a bug, that I
probably want to kill her, that my expression terrifies her and
petrifies her, and that she hopes reaction pleases me, I'm going to
respond and call a spade a spade.

Whether someone is a "communications fanatic" or not is no grounds for
such overly personal revelations of internal processes. As Romana
pointed out, fanaticism is no excuse for such poor manners.

